---
description: "Use shadcn/ui components for all UI code in Bright.Experience"
patterns: "*.tsx"
---

# Shadcn UI Components

This project uses shadcn/ui for UI components. They live in `src/components/ui/`.

## Using Components

```tsx
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"
import { Card, CardContent, CardHeader, CardTitle } from "@/components/ui/card"
import { Badge } from "@/components/ui/badge"
import { Input } from "@/components/ui/input"
```

## Installing Additional Components

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add [component-name]
```

Full list: https://ui.shadcn.com/r

## Class Composition

Always use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes:

```tsx
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"
<div className={cn("base-class", isActive && "active-class")} />
```

## Design System

Bright.Blue design tokens are mapped to shadcn CSS variables in `globals.css`.
Use shadcn's semantic classes (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, etc.)
which automatically render in Bright.Blue brand colours.

The app speaks the **Ink design language** (see `docs/design-language.md`,
the binding style contract): Ink near-black default theme, Ink Light
(`.theme-light`) paper toggle, cobalt→cyan gradient accents
(`.text-brand-gradient`, `.chip-brand-gradient`, `text-brand-cyan`), ambient
corner glows (`.ink-glows`). Semantic tokens only — no `bg-white`,
`slate-*`/`gray-*`, or arbitrary hex on theme-controlled surfaces. One
gradient accent per visual zone; status colours are never gradient.
